# Canonical contributor identities for the ITSA website.
#
# Git counts authors by the exact name+email string on each commit, so one
# person who changes their git config, or commits from a second machine,
# splits into several rows in `git shortlog` and every other author report.
# This file maps those variants back to one identity.
#
# Format:  Proper Name <proper@email>  Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# Nothing is rewritten in history -- .mailmap is a display-time lookup, so it
# is safe to edit at any time and changes no commit hashes.
#
# Adding yourself: if you appear twice below or under a wrong name, add a line
# rather than rewriting history.

